{"content":[{"c":["HUZZAB*"],"sourceClass":"h1","t":"p"},{"c":["Obscure Hebrew word found only in ",{"href":"?bref=Nah.2.7","r":"Nah.2.7","rawR":"Nah.2.7","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Nah.2.7","value":"Nah.2.7"}],"t":"ref","v":"Nahum 2:7"}," (",{"c":["kjv"],"sourceClass":"sc","t":"span"},"). Scholars are uncertain whether the word is a verb meaning “it is decreed,” a noun personifying Nineveh, or a reference to an Assyrian queen. The problem is perhaps due to textual error, but thus far neither textual scholarship nor archaeology has been able to resolve the question."],"sourceClass":"fl","t":"p"}],"format":"bsb-study-dictionary-v2","id":"Huzzab","provenance":{"archiveSha256":"10758ea00dbea7540f9337e43e59c8e4000295c1261e3426bab6f31c31dcff5b","release":"1.6","sourceCitationReferences":[{"anchorText":"Nahum 2:7","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Nah.2.7","rawQueryValue":"Nah.2.7","sourceRefExact":"Nah.2.7"}],"sourceItemFragmentSha256":"f8810fff29df4bf8166a7bf078322d2f4e581fbcad0a08cdfe7abff391d9f050","sourceItemName":"Huzzab","sourceItemOrder":408,"sourceMember":"Articles/H.xml","supplementPointersNotIncludedAsContent":[]},"sourceAttributes":{"name":"Huzzab","product":"TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","typename":"Article"},"sourceTitleExact":"Huzzab*","title":"Huzzab*","version":"v2-a101d843a2f0cd3fc0c6"}